  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Consider the d\u2019Alembert differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}+3(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}).\n$$\n\nIf ${y}^{\u2032}(x)=t,$ then the general solution can be expressed in parametric form $(x(t),y(t)),$ where\n\n$$\ny(t)=(\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|t|-3t+C}{(t-1)^{2}})f(t)+g(t)\n$$\n\nand $C$ is an arbitrary constant. Find $f(t)+g(t).$\n\n*Hint: Under the given transformation, we have*\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{2x}{t-1}=\\frac{3}{t(1-t)}\n$$",
